---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Macro Easy - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Macro Easy"
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/macro-easy/privacy"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-12">Macro Easy &middot; Effective October 22, 2026</p>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Short version</h2>
            <p>Macro Easy keeps your meals and targets on your iPhone. We don't collect, sell or share them. There are no accounts, ads, analytics or tracking.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">What stays on your iPhone</h2>
            <p>The meals you log, your saved meals, your daily targets and your settings are stored on your iPhone, in the app and its widget. They aren't sent to us or anyone else, and there is no server-side copy.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Food search</h2>
            <p>When you search for a food, Macro Easy sends only the words you type to USDA FoodData Central, the U.S. Department of Agriculture's public nutrition database, to get results. Nothing else is sent: not your meals, your targets or anything that identifies you.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Apple Health</h2>
            <p>Apple Health is off until you turn it on in Settings. When it's on, Macro Easy saves the protein, carbohydrates, total fat and dietary energy of each meal you log to Apple Health, and updates or removes them when you edit or delete the meal. Macro Easy never reads your health data. Health data is never used for advertising and never shared with third parties. You can turn it off in Macro Easy, or change what it can write in the Health app.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Deleting your data</h2>
            <p>Delete a meal from its menu, or everything at once in Settings &rarr; Delete all meals. Deleting the app removes everything stored in it.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Contact</h2>
            <p>Privacy questions are welcome at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Macro%20Easy%20Privacy" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
